19.Write a query with a CASE statement that classifies orders as:
High Value (> 1000);Medium Value (500–1000);Low Value (< 500)


select customer_name,price,
CASE
WHEN price > 1000 THEN 'High Value'
        WHEN price BETWEEN 500 AND 1000 THEN 'Medium Value'
        ELSE 'Low Value'
END as saleslevel
from ecommerce_sales;

20.Find month-on-month sales growth using a window function.

select customer_name,product_name, price, 
LAG(price) OVER(order by price desc) as previousmonth,
(price - LAG(price) OVER(order by price)) as salesgrowth,
CASE
when (price - LAG(price) OVER(order by price)) >6 THEN 'increase'
else 'decrease'
end as trends
from ecommerce_sales;
